<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:camunda="http://camunda.org/schema/1.0/bpmn" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_0e3v6wh" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.48.0">
  <bpmn:process id="email-notification-process" name="Email Notification Process" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sends the "received" or "served" notification email to the applicant/contact.

Not called as a callActivity — triggered by message correlation
("message-email-servebc") from VerifyServedDateProcess's SendServedEmailTask,
which sets category/contactEmail/docTypeCode/applicationId as correlation
variables. NotificationRequestStartEvent is asyncBefore=true specifically so
that correlation call returns immediately: a failure anywhere in this
process can never propagate back into VerifyServedDateProcess's transaction.

Flow: Document Type Mapping (DMN) -&gt; Email Template (DMN: resolves
from/bcc/subject/body for the category+documentType) -&gt; Get OAuth Token
(email-specific Keycloak client credentials) -&gt; Invoke email api (POST to
EMAIL_SVC_URL).

Retry design differs between the two integration tasks:
- Get OAuth Token: asyncBefore + failedJobRetryTimeCycle (R3/PT2M) — fetching
  a token has no side effects, safe to auto-retry.
- Invoke email api: asyncBefore, but deliberately NO retry cycle — sending an
  email is not idempotent, so a blind automatic retry risks a duplicate send.
  A stuck job here should be resolved manually (Cockpit "Increment retries"),
  ideally only after confirming with whoever owns the email service whether
  it dedupes by the 'tag' field.

Variables in (via message correlation): category, contactEmail,
applicationId, docTypeCode. Variables set: documentType, template, token,
email_response.

Known gap: both connector tasks are declarative (camunda:connector), not
script tasks, so a technical failure throws a generic exception rather than
a catchable BpmnError — it always becomes a Camunda incident, and there's no
boundary error event anywhere upstream to route it elsewhere.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent" name="End">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:executionListener event="start">
          <camunda:script scriptFormat="javascript">var Logger = Java.type("org.slf4j.LoggerFactory");
var logger = Logger.getLogger("BPMN_SCRIPT");
var timestamp = new java.util.Date().toString();

logger.debug("*********[Notification Email] {} :: {} ::   Notification Email Process Completed with response - {}", timestamp, applicationId, email_response);</camunda:script>
        </camunda:executionListener>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow__invokeemailapi_to_end</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="ReceiveRequestStartEvent" name="Recieve Request" camunda:asyncBefore="true">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:formData>
          <camunda:formField id="category" type="string" />
        </camunda:formData>
        <camunda:executionListener event="start">
          <camunda:script scriptFormat="javascript">var Logger = Java.type("org.slf4j.LoggerFactory");
var logger = Logger.getLogger("BPMN_SCRIPT");
var timestamp = new java.util.Date().toString();

logger.debug("*********[Notification Email] {} :: {} ::   Notification Email Process Started", timestamp, applicationId);</camunda:script>
        </camunda:executionListener>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_start_to_documenttypemapping</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_0o7ax3m" messageRef="Message_1ap8yc0" />
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="EmailTemplateTask" name="Email Template" camunda:asyncAfter="true" camunda:resultVariable="template" camunda:decisionRef="decide-email-template" camunda:mapDecisionResult="singleResult">
      <bpmn:documentation>Setting asynAfter for this element with retry to set the transaction boundary before  the transient email_body variable is set by EmailAttributeListner used later.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:inputOutput>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="category">${category}</camunda:inputParameter>
        </camunda:inputOutput>
        <camunda:failedJobRetryTimeCycle>R3/PT2M</camunda:failedJobRetryTimeCycle>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_documenttypemapping_to_emailtemplate</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_emailtemplate_to_getauthtoken</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_start_to_documenttypemapping" sourceRef="ReceiveRequestStartEvent" targetRef="DocumentTypeMappingTask" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="GetOAuthTokenTask" name="Get OAuth Token">
      <bpmn:documentation>Fetches an email-service access token via client-credentials grant against
EMAIL_KEYCLOAK_URL. Safe to auto-retry (R3/PT2M) since it has no side
effects — see the process documentation for why this differs from
"Invoke email api"'s retry policy.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:connector>
          <camunda:inputOutput>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="url">
              <camunda:script scriptFormat="javascript">var system=java.lang.System;
var emailKcUrl=system.getenv('EMAIL_KEYCLOAK_URL');
emailKcUrl;</camunda:script>
            </camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="method">POST</camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="headers">
              <camunda:map>
                <camunda:entry key="Content-Type">application/x-www-form-urlencoded</camunda:entry>
              </camunda:map>
            </camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="payload">
              <camunda:script scriptFormat="javascript">var system = java.lang.System;
var clientSecret = system.getenv("EMAIL_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET");
var clientId = system.getenv("EMAIL_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID");

var mypayload = `grant_type=client_credentials&amp;client_id=${clientId}&amp;client_secret=${clientSecret}`;
mypayload;</camunda:script>
            </camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:outputParameter name="token">${S(response).prop("access_token").value()}</camunda:outputParameter>
          </camunda:inputOutput>
          <camunda:connectorId>http-connector</camunda:connectorId>
        </camunda:connector>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_emailtemplate_to_getauthtoken</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_getauthtoken_to_invokeemailapi</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_getauthtoken_to_invokeemailapi" sourceRef="GetOAuthTokenTask" targetRef="InvokeEmailApiTask" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="InvokeEmailApiTask" name="Invoke email api" camunda:asyncAfter="true">
      <bpmn:documentation>Sends the actual notification email via EMAIL_SVC_URL. Deliberately has no
failedJobRetryTimeCycle — see the process documentation for why (sending an
email is not idempotent, so blind auto-retry risks a duplicate send).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:connector>
          <camunda:inputOutput>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="payload">
              <camunda:script scriptFormat="javascript">var template = execution.getVariable("template");
var contactEmail = execution.getVariable("contactEmail");
var applicationId = execution.getVariable("applicationId");
var tag = `SL-${applicationId}`;

var payload = {
    from: template.get('from'),
    to: [ contactEmail ],
    bcc: [ template.get('bcc') ],
    bodyType: "html",
    body: email_body,
    subject: email_subject,
    delayTS: "0",
    encoding: "utf-8",
    priority: "normal",
    tag: tag
};

var payloadStr = JSON.stringify(payload);

var logger = Java.type("org.slf4j.LoggerFactory").getLogger("BPMN_SCRIPT");
var timestamp = new java.util.Date().toString();

logger.info("*********[Notification Email] {} :: {} :: Email Tag - {}", timestamp, applicationId, tag);

logger.debug("*********[Notification Email] {} :: {} :: EMAIL API Request - {}", timestamp, applicationId, payloadStr);

payloadStr;</camunda:script>
            </camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="headers">
              <camunda:map>
                <camunda:entry key="accept">application/json</camunda:entry>
                <camunda:entry key="Authorization">Bearer ${token}</camunda:entry>
                <camunda:entry key="Content-Type">application/json</camunda:entry>
              </camunda:map>
            </camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="method">POST</camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:inputParameter name="url">
              <camunda:script scriptFormat="javascript">var system=java.lang.System;
var myurl = system.getenv("EMAIL_SVC_URL");
myurl;</camunda:script>
            </camunda:inputParameter>
            <camunda:outputParameter name="email_response">${response}</camunda:outputParameter>
          </camunda:inputOutput>
          <camunda:connectorId>http-connector</camunda:connectorId>
        </camunda:connector>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_getauthtoken_to_invokeemailapi</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow__invokeemailapi_to_end</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow__invokeemailapi_to_end" sourceRef="InvokeEmailApiTask" targetRef="EndEvent" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_documenttypemapping_to_emailtemplate" sourceRef="DocumentTypeMappingTask" targetRef="EmailTemplateTask" />
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="DocumentTypeMappingTask" name="Document Type Mapping" camunda:resultVariable="documentType" camunda:decisionRef="servebc-documenttype-mapping" camunda:mapDecisionResult="singleEntry">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:inputOutput>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="docTypeCode">${docTypeCode}</camunda:inputParameter>
        </camunda:inputOutput>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_start_to_documenttypemapping</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_documenttypemapping_to_emailtemplate</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_emailtemplate_to_getauthtoken" sourceRef="EmailTemplateTask" targetRef="GetOAuthTokenTask">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:executionListener class="org.camunda.bpm.extension.hooks.listeners.execution.EmailAttributesListener" event="take" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmn:message id="Message_1ap8yc0" name="message-email-servebc" />
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="email-notification-process">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_0k4s884_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent">
        <dc:Bounds x="862" y="99" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="870" y="142" width="20" height="14" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_1qc25qm_di" bpmnElement="ReceiveRequestStartEvent">
        <dc:Bounds x="182" y="99" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="159" y="142" width="84" height="14" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="BusinessRuleTask_02kbmdk_di" bpmnElement="EmailTemplateTask">
        <dc:Bounds x="410" y="77" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Activity_1lxtect_di" bpmnElement="GetOAuthTokenTask">
        <dc:Bounds x="570" y="77" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Activity_1rniyh0_di" bpmnElement="InvokeEmailApiTask">
        <dc:Bounds x="720" y="77" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Activity_1a6wgpn_di" bpmnElement="DocumentTypeMappingTask">
        <dc:Bounds x="270" y="77" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="SequenceFlow_01shpg1_di" bpmnElement="flow_start_to_documenttypemapping">
        <di:waypoint x="218" y="117" />
        <di:waypoint x="270" y="117" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_14n17ln_di" bpmnElement="flow_getauthtoken_to_invokeemailapi">
        <di:waypoint x="670" y="117" />
        <di:waypoint x="720" y="117" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_1o80ruh_di" bpmnElement="flow__invokeemailapi_to_end">
        <di:waypoint x="820" y="117" />
        <di:waypoint x="862" y="117" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_0gv8qf7_di" bpmnElement="flow_documenttypemapping_to_emailtemplate">
        <di:waypoint x="370" y="117" />
        <di:waypoint x="410" y="117" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_0br2jt8_di" bpmnElement="flow_emailtemplate_to_getauthtoken">
        <di:waypoint x="510" y="117" />
        <di:waypoint x="570" y="117" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
